{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791601358,"nonce":"dy6qZCI/HK7bqzK355zx9k1eTKM=","message":"Decision: one rejection is one application. Rejections (email and manual rows alike) are paired with at most one applied application by group, else employer plus title (blank title matches any); unpaired ones count once as applied elsewhere, deduped by employer and title. Near-title groups of a rejected posting are left out of the flows and never counted as applications. Reason: one email was counted as up to 55 applications; Fluidstack was both awaiting and rejected. Manual rejection rows with no job are now counted too (before only email rows were); they also prove an application.","files":null}]}